				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## Barry window title\nOwner: CatalystDevKit, BV-Catalyst-Fairy-Core (GT/Pharo UI only). Related contract: [[Catalyst framework ownership]], [[Catalyst working rules]], [[Catalyst Fairy]].\n\nCatalyst's world spawn handler gives BVCFairyChat windows the stable title `Barry`, both before and after messages. Ordinary GT chats delegate unchanged to the inherited handler. The only production selector added is {{gtMethod:BVCDevKitWorldElement>>#onGtPhlowObjectToSpawn:}}, an extension owned by BV-Catalyst-Fairy-Core. Existing chat tools, composite tabs and pager construction are reused; no replacement dispatcher or chat tool was added."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-10-18T09:13:21.069382+11:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-10-18T09:13:21.069382+11:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "emTwBAdYRBCYZRchO7eGeg=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## Inspected path and scope\nThe Add chat button creates a registered chat and fires a GtPhlowObjectToSpawn carrying its default inspector tool. GtLChat>>gtDefaultInspectorTool already names the composite; BVCFairyChat>>gtDisplayOn: already includes Barry. Neither is the missing window title source. GtWorldElement>>onGtPhlowObjectToSpawn: creates a BlSpace with inPager: but supplies no title; BlSpace's default title is empty. The Catalyst subclass now sets the title before using that same pager/showFrom: path. GtWorldTabElement>>createBaseTab: copies BlSpace>>title into the tab label. Opening the resulting space natively propagates the title to the host window.\n\nThe separate GtLWorldRegistrySubscriptionHandler path already sets a display-based title and is unchanged. GtLWorldChatRegistryDropdown>>initialize still forwards the spawn without consuming the original. The upstream duplicate-window issue is intentionally untouched. A BVCFairyChat-only display or tool-name override would not repair the world handler's missing title assignment."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-10-18T09:13:21.078309+11:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-10-18T09:13:21.078309+11:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "yWuKEzR9RLiVlsq/tSbCPg=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## Current-image checks\nExecuted in SuperGame.image, Pharo13.1.0SNAPSHOT, native BlWinitHost. Final BVCFairyWindowTitleExamples run: 4 successes, 0 failures, 0 errors, 0 skips. Checks cover a newly registered Catalyst chat through world phlow spawn, BlSpace title and tab-label propagation, retained and reopened titles after an offline message, unchanged ordinary GT chat behavior, and the real native host-space title before/after a message. The native example closes its window and checks closure with a 5-second bound. Temporary world tabs and mocked scripter scene children are removed in ensure: blocks; no live provider calls.\n\nExisting popupCreatesCatalystChat also passed (1); GtPhlowChatToolExamples passed all 6 examples with no failures/errors/skips. These are focused checks, not a full DevKit suite. Initial example-authoring runs exposed incorrect test selectors and an incorrect assumption that BlScripterSpace could report closed; corrected before the final green run. BlScripterSpace uses a mocked host and reports open whenever its host exists, so cleanup asserts an empty scene and no host space instead.\n\nExcluded: end-to-end duplicate dropdown-window counts, native title-bar pixels/OS chrome, other platforms, fresh BVC build, source-file save, commit and push. Source changes remain in the image."
			},
